# EXECUTION PROTOCOL

## STEP 1 — CLASSIFY
Is this question atomic (single lookup) or does it need decomposition?

Atomic triggers: one file, one table, one cell, no computation.
Non-atomic triggers: multiple bulletins, computation required, external values needed,
visual reasoning, temporal comparison, fiscal year interpretation.

If atomic → go to STEP 3 directly.
If non-atomic → go to STEP 2.

## STEP 2 — PLAN (if non-atomic)

Decompose into minimum subtasks. Use these typed subtask labels:
- [RETRIEVE_TABLE]: Extract value from markdown table in transformed/*.txt
- [RETRIEVE_TEXT]: Find footnotes, headers, qualifiers
- [RETRIEVE_EXTERNAL]: Get values not in Treasury docs (CPI, GDP, etc.)
- [RETRIEVE_VISUAL]: Extract from charts/graphs in PDFs
- [THINK_MATH]: Compute from extracted values
- [THINK_DISAMBIGUATE]: Resolve fiscal vs calendar year, net vs gross, etc.

Rules:
- ALWAYS start with RETRIEVE to find the right file(s)
- Separate extraction from computation
- Max 6 subtasks. Max depth 2 (plan once, execute leaves).
- For fiscal year questions: add THINK_DISAMBIGUATE first.

## STEP 3 — EXECUTE (for each subtask)

For every RETRIEVE task, produce an EVIDENCE CARD (not prose):
```
EVIDENCE_CARD:
  value: <base number, no commas/$/%>
  unit_header: "<exact unit text from table header>"
  base_number_only: true
  source_file: <filename>
  table_key: "<row label> / <column label>"
  raw_snippet: "<2-3 lines of source context>"
  confidence: high|medium|low
```

For THINK_MATH tasks:
```
EVIDENCE_CARD:
  value: <computed result>
  method: "<formula>"
  inputs: {name: value, ...}
  computation: "<step-by-step>"
  confidence: high|medium|low
```

Formulas reference:
- Percentage change: (new - old) / old × 100
- CAGR: (end/start)^(1/n) - 1
- Geometric mean: exp(mean(ln(values)))
- Coefficient of variation: (std / mean) × 100

## STEP 4 — AGGREGATE (if there were subtasks)

Consume ONLY evidence cards. Check:
- All cards have base_number_only: true
- Units are consistent across cards
- Magnitude makes sense for era (pre-1950: thousands-millions; post-2000: billions-trillions)

## STEP 5 — VERIFY (mandatory before final answer)

Run the scorer-mirror checklist:

□ UNIT_EXPANSION: Does my answer have more digits than the source value? → expanded units
□ CORRECT_CELL: Row AND column labels match the question exactly?
□ CORRECT_FILE: Filename year/month matches the question?
□ FISCAL_YEAR: If fiscal year, correct boundary? (before 1977: Jul-Jun; after: Oct-Sep)
□ FORMAT: No commas, no $, no %, correct sign, source precision?
□ COMPLETENESS: For multi-number answers, ALL values present?
□ MAGNITUDE: Number reasonable for era and category?

If ANY check fails → go back to the failing step, fix, re-verify (max 1 retry).

## STEP 6 — OUTPUT

```
FINAL_ANSWER: <base number or text+number>
```

# COMMON TRAPS

- "In millions" = number IS ALREADY in millions — DON'T multiply
- Fiscal year ≠ calendar year (before 1977: Jul-Jun; after 1977: Oct-Sep; TQ: Jul-Sep 1976)
- Later bulletins revise earlier numbers — use the bulletin the question specifies
- "Net" vs "gross" — read qualifiers carefully
- Multi-page tables: check for "(Continued)" headers
- Scorer tolerance is 0.00 by default — be exact
- OCR artifacts: l↔1, O↔0, (123)→-123
